{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/205294-local-chapters-of-compacts-conspiracies","id":205294,"title":"Local \"Chapters\" of Compacts/Conspiracies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T13:37:18-07:00","id":205294,"title":"Local \"Chapters\" of Compacts/Conspiracies","content":"Some of the Compacts and most of the Conspiracies exist in multiple cities, while a few hold their Vigil across the entire globe. It would be boring (and probably incorrect!) to assume that the Long Night is the same in Los Angeles as it is in Salem, or that the VALKYRIE department in Alaska is the same as the one that watches over the Southwest. While largely the same organization as the whole, this thread is for sharing examples of the regional flavor for different Compacts/Conspiracies. I'll start with one I'm using for my upcoming Changeling game, <i>Arkham Lost</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arkham has a fair number of old families with deep roots, those who made their fortunes off the sea and now inhabit tumbledown manors in the historic part of town along the river. Many of these families are known for their eccentricities, but the locals know better than to pry or simply do not care. Generations of wealth and prestige mingle at gatherings of the local branch of the Ashwood Abbey, which masquerades as a yacht club but is known by its membership as the Black Goat Society. The club is almost exclusively of the Libertine clique, engaged in the endless pursuit of hedonism and taboo, but those of the Arkham branch have something that distinguishes them from their peers across the world: the Black Goat.<br /> <br /> Carved from some sort of dark volcanic rock, the Black Goat is a life-sized idol of a hermaphroditic figure with some figures of a goat. Members either find it intensely alluring or wholly repulsive; there is no middle reaction, and those who find themselves feeling the latter are doomed to low Status within the Abbey within Arkham. For those who care for such things, the Black Goat is either Pan or Baphomet, a divinity pushing them to further excess. The idol is brought to all Abbey gatherings, be they bacchanal parties or their cruel hunts; it is considered good luck to grope the idol before setting out to kill or capture a monster.<br /> <br /> Those with high Status (4+) are invited to secret meetings that are little more than orgies cloaked in a bunch of showy faux-occultism on the night of the New Moon. The revelers do have one bit of real magic up their sleeves, however; they invoke the Black Goat's name (none remember it before or after these events, only during the height of ecstasy) and invite it to step down from its pedestal. The beast then parties the night away, pushing the members of the Abbey to higher and higher peaks of filthy debauchery and callous sadism. It has an appetite all its own, and will often take lovers from the Abbey; pregnancies often result, which come to term with impossible speed before ending, suddenly, without a birth, the child taken from the womb by the Black Goat.<br /> <br /> None of the other local hunter elements (Delta Green, the Long Night) know of the Black Goat Society as anything other than a group of rich swingers with too much time on their hands. If word were to somehow escape about the idol and what it does, both they and the Sons of Summer would stop at nothing to destroy it and those whose lives it has tainted. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T14:53:58-07:00","id":205357,"title":"","content":"<i>This is complete headcanon for a Mage game I\u2019m in; my character was a member of the Maiden\u2019s Blood sisterhood in her youth, leaving after an injury took her out of the game (she was too proud to take a \u2018desk job\u2019, and later Awakened and became a badass again in that way).</i><br /> <br /> The Asheville, North Carolina branch of the Maiden\u2019s Blood Sisterhood is more strongly represented by the Pi Alpha Kappa sorority at UNCA (The University of North Carolina \u2013 Asheville) than by Sister Shelters and outreach programs\u2014in fact, there\u2019s only a single Shelter in the town. On the whole, despite being relatively close to the New England roots of the Compact, the Asheville Sisters are significantly younger than the compact\u2019s average age. There\u2019s a history of members moving up north after graduation, which, combined with a prevailing attitude among those who remain that membership during college is \u2018serving one\u2019s time\u2019, means there\u2019s no consistent leadership, and instead a tradition of the graduating members passing on the torch to the next year\u2019s heads.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, this is represented by the fact that Compact Status only reaches up to 3 in Asheville. Occasionally ranking Mothers and Crones from neighboring chapters show up, either to recruit or to gather strength for a problem of regional threat, but no Sister in Asheville can gain the 4<sup>th</sup> dot of Status. There simply isn\u2019t a supporting structure for that level of power within the town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T21:17:26-08:00","id":315053,"title":"","content":"TFV's COLUMBIA Unit in Washington, DC, have become too bloated for their own good. Currently the makeup is four mixed cells of TWILIGHT operatives, three of Suit-only ADAMSKI agents, and one Suit/SWAT FORT cell. Their primary focus has always been on the primary government buildings, from the Congressional office blocks to the White House to the Pentagon across the river. They're constantly armed with the best gear and equipment, but the FORT agents are constantly pointing out how little is done to study the paranormal map of the city. Instead, the ADAMSKI cells have been pulled into the clusterfuck that is the NSA in Fort Meade and the TWILIGHT cells are constantly being pulled from brushfire to brushfire every night and day to keep the status quo. This has left the FORT operatives grasping desperately for help, and right into the arms of Division Six. Unwilling to mention the organization to their sister cells yet for fear of interrupting another cover operation, FORT has instead started to try and open a small but growing rapport with the group in the hopes of gathering some information on the city's P/S-ENE population. No fools, they have at least put in for information with command as to who, exactly, is running the division, but as bureaucracy will always be bureaucracy, that answer is snaking its slow path to the leadership of the conspiracy one day at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T23:36:06-08:00","id":315093,"title":"","content":"What's New York City look like in your Hunter games in terms of the representation? The notes I've been working on suggest that TFV is probably present in a very observational capacity, viewing NYC as a Petri dish of ENE activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:02:01-08:00","id":315794,"title":"","content":"<i>We're in the Union. That used to mean something, but its been a long time since then. The Union got busted, the jobs went away and the city itself is rotten to the core. We used to be steel workers, car makers, refinery workers, dock laborers and even the people who picked up your garbage. Now we're the old timers dreaming of what it used to be like. The next generation moves on to Ann Arbor if they're smart, to the street if they're dumb; the Union is dying. Sure, we had a few jump-starts and surges ahead, but the city has rusted through the framework and we can't find our footing. Kids these days just send pictures and talk, using their cell phones and their computers; people taking notes on how a city dies. I hope it makes a good read, because while the kids watch, us old-timers are bleeding in the streets. Broken, bloody and too old for this, the Union ain't dead yet and neither is Detroit.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}